        solution: "<strong>Expected flow:</strong><br><br>1. <code>=SD</code> + Enter → SDSF Primary Menu. <code>DA</code> + Enter → Display Active panel.<br>2. Sample DA panel rows (showing CICS regions among other STCs):<pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:1rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.45;margin:.6rem 0;\">JOBNAME    STEPNAME PROCSTEP JOBID    OWNER    C   POS-DP REAL  PAGING SIO    CPU%\nCICSAOR1   CICSAOR1 CICS     STC12345 CICSUSR  STC IN   FE       12K     0   0.4   1.20\nCICSAOR2   CICSAOR2 CICS     STC12346 CICSUSR  STC IN   FE       12K     0   0.6   2.10\nCICSTOR1   CICSTOR1 CICS     STC12347 CICSUSR  STC IN   FE        8K     0   0.3   0.45\nTCPIP      TCPIP    TCPIP    STC12100 TCPIP    STC IN   FE        6K     0   0.0   0.12\nVTAM       NET      NET      STC12101 NET      STC IN   FE        4K     0   0.0   0.08\n...</pre>3. Type S next to CICSAOR1 + Enter → DD list. Look for: STEPLIB (the CICS nucleus library, typically CICSTSnn.SDFHAUTH), DFHRPL (application load libraries — concatenated PDS or PDSE list), and the standard JES* DDs.<br>4. S on JESJCL → see EXEC PGM=DFHSIP, plus all the SYSIN initialization parameters.<br>5. S on JESMSGLG → look for the startup chain:<pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:.6rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.85rem;margin:.4rem 0;\">DFHSI1500 CICSAOR1 CICS startup is in progress for CICS Transaction Server Version 5.6.0\nDFHTR0103 TRACE TABLE SIZE IS 64K\nDFHSM0122I CICSAOR1 Limit of DSA storage below 16MB is 5,120K\nDFHKE0408I CICSAOR1 Activated 10 of 64 system tasks\nDFHSI1502I CICSAOR1 Initialization complete for system 'CICSAOR1'\nDFHSI1517 CICSAOR1 Control is being given to CICS\n...\nDFHTS0001 TS - Temporary Storage initialization completed\nDFHTM1715 CICSAOR1 Terminal control is initialized\n... (steady state operation thereafter)</pre>The DFHSI1517 message is the 'fully ready' marker — anything before it represents the startup phase; subsequent DFH messages are runtime events.<br><br><strong>What you've learned:</strong> (a) CICS regions are normal z/OS started tasks running PGM=DFHSIP; (b) the JCL identifies the CICS release and points at the application code via DFHRPL; (c) startup is a multi-phase process visible in JESMSGLG with DFH-prefixed messages; (d) the DFHSI1517 line marks transition to steady-state operation. From here, problems anywhere in the region's life show up as DFH messages with severity codes (I=informational, W=warning, E=error). Filter with FIND 'DFHSI' or 'DFHME' to triage."
