        solution: "<strong>Sign-on:</strong><pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:.6rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.85rem;margin:.4rem 0;\">CESN\nUSERID  ===&gt; Z12345\nPASSWORD ===&gt; ********\n\nDFHCE3520 SIGN-ON IS COMPLETE</pre><strong>CECI session — try a few harmless inquiries:</strong><pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:1rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.45;margin:.6rem 0;\">CECI ASKTIME ABSTIME(W)\n\n   COMMAND    : EXEC CICS ASKTIME ABSTIME(W)\n  +000  +ABSTIME      = 0140012345678\n   RESPONSE   : NORMAL                 EIBRESP=+0000000000  EIBRESP2=+0000000000</pre>That ABSTIME value is the millisecond count since 1900-01-01. Not human-readable; CICS programs typically pass it to FORMATTIME for display.<pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:1rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.45;margin:.6rem 0;\">CECI INQUIRE PROGRAM(CESN)\n\n   COMMAND    : EXEC CICS INQUIRE PROGRAM(CESN)\n   PROGRAM     ( CESN     )\n   LANGUAGE    ( ASSEMBLER )\n   STATUS      ( ENABLED   )\n   USECOUNT    ( +0000003421 )\n   ENTRYPOINT  ( 081A2330  )\n   LENGTH      ( +0000045088 )\n   RESPONSE   : NORMAL</pre>Tells you about the CESN sign-on program itself: it's an assembler module, currently enabled, has been called 3421 times since region start.<pre style=\"background:#0d0d0d;color:#ffb000;padding:1rem;border-radius:4px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:'Share Tech Mono',monospace;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.45;margin:.6rem 0;\">CECI WRITEQ TS QUEUE('TESTQ001') FROM('hello from CECI')\n\n   COMMAND    : EXEC CICS WRITEQ TS QUEUE('TESTQ001') FROM('hello from CECI')\n   RESPONSE   : NORMAL\n\nCECI READQ TS QUEUE('TESTQ001') INTO(D)\n\n   COMMAND    : EXEC CICS READQ TS QUEUE('TESTQ001') INTO(D)\n  +000  +D = hello from CECI\n   RESPONSE   : NORMAL</pre>Just wrote and read back from a Temporary Storage queue named TESTQ001 without writing any application code.<br><br><strong>Cleanup:</strong> CECI DELETEQ TS QUEUE('TESTQ001') removes the queue; CESF signs off.<br><br><strong>What you've learned:</strong> CECI lets you exercise CICS commands interactively — perfect for learning the API, debugging a command before embedding it in code, or doing one-off operational fixes (e.g., 'enable this program: <code>CECI SET PROGRAM(MYAPP) ENABLED</code>'). The EIBRESP and EIBRESP2 fields in the response are the canonical CICS error-condition mechanism — every EXEC CICS call sets them; non-zero usually means trouble.<br><br><strong>If no CICS region is available</strong> on your system, this task can be done as reading-only: the IBM Knowledge Center has the full EXEC CICS command reference, and the DOGECICS GitHub example (referenced in Sources) shows the equivalent commands embedded in a real COBOL application."
